        // The generator itself doesn't automatically know when the outer caller stops calling next() 
        // UNLESS we wrap the logic in a way that respects the `done` flag of the *current* step? No.
        // The standard way to handle cleanup in an async generator when the consumer stops early is to rely on the fact that 
